{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":196,"description":"The `includeDraft` flag is added to `ICreateQueryConfig` and `ICreateEntryConfig` and handled inside `ContentstackFactory`, but none of the public-facing functions (`getEntry`, `getSingleEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`) accept or propagate `includeDraft` to the factory. Their corresponding interfaces (`IContentstackGetEntry`, `IContentstackGetSingleEntry`, `IContentstackGetSingletonEntry`) have no `includeDraft` field. This means the `includeDraft` parameter is dead code — no caller can ever set it to `true`, so draft content will never be served. All three acceptance criteria (draft in preview, live update without rebuild, published outside preview) are unmet because the preview flag never reaches the query.","suggestedFix":"Add `includeDraft?: boolean` to `IContentstackPageConfig` (or `IContentstackGetEntry`) so it propagates through `IContentstackGetSingleEntry` and `IContentstackGetSingletonEntry`. Then in each public function (`getEntry`, `getSingleEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`), pass `includeDraft` from the function args into the factory call: `factory.createContentTypeQuery({ ..., includeDraft })` and `factory.createContentTypeEntryQuery({ ..., includeDraft })`."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/pages","line":0,"description":"No page-level `getStaticProps` (or any caller) passes `context.preview` through to the contentstack service calls. The prescribed fix states: 'Propagate preview flag from getStaticProps context (context.preview) through to these factory methods.' This propagation is entirely missing — no page reads `context.preview` and passes `includeDraft: true` to `getEntry`/`getSingleEntry`/`getSingletonEntry`. Without this, the CMS preview experience will never display draft content.","suggestedFix":"In each page's `getStaticProps`, read `context.preview` and pass `includeDraft: Boolean(context.preview)` to the contentstack service calls. Alternatively, create a shared helper (e.g. in `services/contentstack.ts`) that wraps the preview flag extraction from Next.js context."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests were added for the live preview / includeDraft functionality. The diff only modifies existing test files (removing date/insertDate assertions from unrelated email-sign-up tests). There are zero tests verifying that `includeDraft: true` causes `addParam('include_draft', 'true')` to be called, or that `includeDraft: false`/omitted does not. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests mirroring the src/ path.","suggestedFix":"Add `src/__tests__/services/contentstack.spec.ts` (or similar) with tests that: (1) mock the Stack and verify `addParam('include_draft', 'true')` is called when `includeDraft` is passed; (2) verify it is NOT called when omitted; (3) verify the `live_preview` config is applied to the Stack when env vars are present."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":150,"description":"The `query.toJSON()` call is now separated from the query chain and its return value is discarded. In the original code, `.toJSON()` was chained and returned the query for further chaining. Now `query.toJSON()` is called as a standalone statement (line 153/155), and subsequent calls like `query.includeCount()`, `query.skip()`, `query.where()` operate on the original query object. While this may work if the SDK mutates in place, the discarded return value is fragile and differs from the SDK's intended fluent API usage. If `.toJSON()` returns a new wrapper, subsequent calls won't take effect.","suggestedFix":"Reorder so `.toJSON()` is called last (after all param additions), or capture its return: `const query = this.stack.ContentType(contentTypeUid).Query().language(lang); if (includeDraft) query.addParam('include_draft', 'true'); ... return query.toJSON();` — ensuring `.toJSON()` is the terminal call returning the final query object."},{"severity":"minor","file":"orchestrations/agents/KB.md","line":1,"description":"A new `KB.md` file is added under `orchestrations/agents/` which appears to be agent orchestration metadata, not project source code. This file should not be committed to the repository as it is tooling artifact, not application code.","suggestedFix":"Remove `orchestrations/agents/KB.md` from the commit or add it to `.gitignore`."}],"summary":"The implementation adds the `includeDraft` flag to the Contentstack factory methods and interfaces, and configures `live_preview` on the Stack initialization. However, the change is incomplete: the `includeDraft` parameter is never propagated through the public-facing functions (`getEntry`, `getSingleEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`, `getSingletonEntry`) — their interfaces lack the field and the functions don't pass it to the factory. No page-level `getStaticProps` passes `context.preview` through. Consequently, the flag is dead code and none of the three acceptance criteria (draft display in preview, live update without rebuild, published content outside preview) are actually achievable. Additionally, no unit tests were added for this feature. The `.toJSON()` call ordering is also potentially fragile. Verdict: changes_requested."}
